              "disposition": "new_distinct_ingredient_proposal",
              "reasoning": "OriginalCCAPN75S specifies1g Cerophyll cereal grass leaves from Ward's per liter. It boils the powdered leaves in75%seawater for5minutes, restores volume, filters and autoclaves. Both frozen algae and MediaDiveC61-derived recipes describe this material/preparation. A whole-leaf input and its filtered infusion are distinct stages; a generic grass taxon or cellulose is not an exact ingredient identity. Original CCAP identifies Ward's Cerophyll cereal grass leaves as the powdered input to N75S. This establishes a named supplier-associated biological material; no specific cereal species, chemical composition or equivalence with the finished filtered infusion is inferred. The existing unqualified Cerophyll owner from MediaDive2360 is a potential same-product candidate, but its complete source context does not establish the Ward's preparation here; coordinator must reconcile before integration without an automatic merge. Context-only source labels are retained as non-resolving REJECTED_LABEL; RAW_TEXT source annotations alone do not enforce that scope.",
              "applicability": "Individually reviewed source case 35: 'Cerophyll cereal grass leaves'; all 2 original occurrence IDs and full frozen recipe contexts are retained in RS-035-FROZEN. Primary references are scoped to those exact recipes or explicitly identified chemical/product candidates; no identity or concentration is transferred to a different preparation. This review preserves every inherited source/native hold and does not approve roles or release.",
